  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Morning Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    28 July 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good morning Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,218.88/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>HONEYWELL</td>\n                <td>₦1,220.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,218.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>LISTER</td>\n                <td>₦1,219.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AIPEC</td>\n                <td>₦1,218.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>11PLC</td>\n                <td>₦1,218.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,220.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,218.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SHEMA</td>\n                <td>₦1,220.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,633.75/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MENJ</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AIPEC</td>\n                <td>₦1,635.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,625.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,635.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,635.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Sink for Fourth Consecutive Day as U.S.-Iran Tensions Continue to Ease\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude traded at $87.11 per barrel, down 1.41 per cent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) slipped 1.28 per cent to $81.55 per barrel. The latest decline came after a fourth consecutive night passed without fresh attacks by either Washington or Tehran.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-sink-for-fourth-consecutive-day-as-us-iran-tensions-continue-to-ease\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Cooking Gas Prices Fall Further as Massive LPG Imports Boost Supply\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria's cooking gas market is showing stronger signs of price moderation as increased imports continue to boost product availability. Recent market checks indicate that retail LPG prices have declined steadily across parts of Abuja over the past three weeks.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/cooking-gas-prices-fall-further-as-massive-lpg-imports-boost-supply\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Fuel Prices Hold Firm Despite Nearly 7% Drop in Global Crude Oil\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                     Depot fuel prices across Nigeria remained unchanged on Monday despite a nearly 7 percent decline in global crude oil prices. Checks by Petroleumprice.ng showed that depot prices remained stable across major supply locations. The stable depot pricing means marketers and bulk buyers continue to purchase products at the same rates.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-fuel-prices-hold-firm-despite-nearly-7-drop-in-global-crude-oil\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Drop Nearly 7% as Brent Falls to $90 on Iran Truce Hopes\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Global oil prices fell nearly 7 percent on Monday, dragging Brent crude down to $90 per barrel. The decline reflects growing optimism that diplomatic efforts could prevent a wider regional conflict. Despite the sharp fall in crude prices, energy markets remain cautious as major shipping routes continue to face operational risks.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-drop-nearly-7-as-brent-falls-to-90-on-iran-truce-hopes\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Says Naira Petrol Sales Resumed to Prevent Fuel Scarcity\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Dangote Petroleum Refinery has disclosed that its decision to resume the sale of Premium Motor Spirit (PMS) in naira was driven by the need to avert a potential fuel shortage. A senior management official of the refinery, who spoke on condition of anonymity, said the decision was taken to stabilise the domestic market. The disclosure comes days after the refinery abandoned its short-lived dollar-denominated pricing regime.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-says-naira-petrol-sales-resumed-to-prevent-fuel-scarcity\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
